From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: leds: qcom-lpg: describe the PMXR2230 PWM block

The Uke OEM PMXR2230 description uses the same four PWM channel offsets,
tri-LED enable register and channel masks as the PM8350C LPG descriptor.
Describe its identity with that existing fallback. Board routing and visible
color support are independent of the peripheral compatibility declaration.

This is a source candidate; it is not part of the admitted kernel patch set.
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/leds-qcom-lpg.yaml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/leds-qcom-lpg.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/leds-qcom-lpg.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/leds-qcom-lpg.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/leds-qcom-lpg.yaml
@@ -44,6 +44,7 @@ properties:
           - enum:
               - qcom,pm8550-pwm
               - qcom,pmh0101-pwm
+              - qcom,pmxr2230-pwm
           - const: qcom,pm8350c-pwm
       - items:
           - enum:
